# The Conservatory's door on orchid (issue #9): https://conservatory.lan,
# one site block for orchid's Caddy. The Aviary's config
# (project-squirrel/Servers/Caddyfile-orchid, hand-synced to
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile) is not touched; it takes this file in with one line
# at its END, after the lan_tls snippet is defined:
#
#     import /home/todd/conservatory/Servers/Caddyfile.conservatory
#
# then `sudo systemctl reload caddy`. Same manual-sync posture as every other
# Caddy change in the house: a reverse-proxy config that deploys itself on
# merge could take every web surface down at once, so a merge that changes
# this file is followed by a reload by hand.
#
# lan_tls is the house snippet: the private root's certificate, HSTS, and
# compression at the choke point (route JSON and page HTML; images pass
# through untouched). The name needs a Pi-hole Local DNS record,
# conservatory.lan -> 192.168.1.148, on pearl's Pi-hole and on orchid's
# standby copy. 3010 is the web unit's port; 3000 is the Aviary's.

conservatory, conservatory.lan {
	import lan_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3010
}
